libnv: name/value lists (nvlist), NPF's configuration and ioctl format.

Source:		NetBSD-10 sys/external/bsd/libnv/dist (last changed there in
		cafa3bdb039, 2024-09-05), itself FreeBSD's libnv.
License:	BSD-2-Clause (file headers).

Local changes (MINIX):
- dist/nv.h: the nvlist_ref_t/nvlist_t definitions taken for NetBSD are
  taken for MINIX too (`#if defined(__NetBSD__) || defined(__minix)`).

Elsewhere libnv still tests __NetBSD__ alone.  In particular nvlist.c and
nvpair.c leave descriptor (NV_TYPE_DESCRIPTOR*) packing and unpacking out
on NetBSD only, so a MINIX userland build, the lwip service included (it
is not _KERNEL), has them.  Unpacking still rejects every descriptor while
no descriptors are passed in (nvlist_unpack() passes none); revisit this
before nvlists from user ioctls are unpacked with descriptors (NPF does
not use them).

Tests: minix/tests/npfdeps/nvlist_*_test.c are the unmodified unit tests
of https://github.com/rmind/nvlist (commit 551f171, 2019-04-15), built
against these sources (as NetBSD's external/bsd/libnv/lib/srcs.mk).

To update: copy NetBSD's dist/ over dist/, then re-apply the change above.
